# pointer-identity: Git LFS files are admitted by their pointer blob (sha256 oid + size),
# already bound by each source's commit and tree SHA, and are never downloaded, so the
# closure never depends on an LFS endpoint, quota, or credentials.
cc:lfsObjectPolicy a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
